{"additions":3173,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nA read-only **Actions** page (key `6`) for GitHub Actions on top of `gh run …`, reusing the GitHub page's plumbing (`gh` detection, background fetch, disk cache, browser open):\n\n- **Runs** — `gh run list --limit 50 --json …`: status icon (queued / in progress / success / failure / cancelled / skipped), workflow, `#number`, branch, event, duration (elapsed while running) and age. While any run is queued or in progress the list refreshes every 5 s. `/` searches workflow / branch / event, `o` opens the run in the browser, the selection drives the jobs pane.\n- **Jobs** — `gh run view <id> --json jobs` as a `job → steps` tree via `core::tree::nest_by`; status icon and duration per row, failed steps in red. `Enter` / `i` opens the job's log (from a step row the log scrolls to that step); jobs of an active run are re-fetched every 5 s.\n- **Log** — `gh run view <id> --log --job <job>` in the shared `TailPane`; step boundaries and `##[group]` markers as section lines, `##[error]` / `##[warning]` colored, `]` / `[` jump between failed steps, `/` search, `G` resumes following. Running jobs fall back to the REST job-log endpoint (`gh api …/actions/jobs/<id>/logs`) and are polled every 5 s with new lines appended; one final fetch when the job completes. No extra secret filtering (GitHub masks with `***`).\n\nNothing reruns, cancels or deletes anything.\n\nCloses #98, closes #99, closes #100, closes #101, closes #102\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/actions/` — `page.rs`, `state.rs` (`ActionsState`, `ActionsBgMessage`, polling in `on_tick`), `domain/{client,types,time,log}.rs`, `panes/{runs,jobs,log}.rs`\n- `assets/default.kdl` — `page \"actions\"` block and `\"6\" \"page:actions\"`\n- `src/main.rs`, `src/core/app.rs` (test), `src/core/config/loader.rs` (`actions_page()` + test), `src/core/ui/status_bar.rs` (header / status bar)\n- `src/github/domain/{client,disk_cache}.rs` — `run_gh` / `run_gh_json` / cache helpers made `pub(crate)` for reuse (no behavior change)\n- `README.md`, `docs/README.ja.md`, `docs/config.md`, `mise.toml` (`demo:actions`, added to `demo:all`)\n- `tape/demo-actions.tape` + `assets/demo-actions.gif`\n\nUnit tests cover run / jobs JSON fixtures, `RunState` derivation, ISO 8601 parsing, duration / relative-time formatting, log line and section parsing (both `gh run view --log` columns and REST output), failed-step jumps, append-vs-replace polling, selection preservation and pane events.\n\n## Page order\n\nThis PR appends the Actions page after Docker (`pages = [git, github, files, docker, actions]`). The Procs (key 5) and Worktrees (key 7) PRs append theirs the same way; the final order should be **git, github, files, docker, procs, actions, worktrees**. The help overlay's view-switch entry on this page reads `1 … 7`; the other pages' entries (`1 / 2 / 3 / 4`) are left for the merge that sets the final order.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- Log polling of a job that is actually in progress (no run was in progress while testing); the REST fallback was exercised against a completed job only, and its append / final-fetch logic is unit-tested.\n- The GIF was recorded against td72/vig's real runs; the header shows the page as `5:Actions` in this branch alone because tab labels are positional.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":25,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-28T08:36:57Z","deletions":9,"headRefName":"feat/actions-view","labels":[],"number":112,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPfM6w","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere is a confirmed correctness issue in the new ISO8601 parser (`parse_iso8601`) where impossible dates are treated as valid, which can lead to incorrect time calculations.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR adds a new read-only **Actions** page to vig (switchable via key `6`) that surfaces GitHub Actions workflow runs, their jobs/steps, and per-job logs by calling `gh run …` / `gh api …`, reusing the existing GitHub page’s `gh` plumbing and disk cache.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Introduces a new `src/actions/` page with panes for Runs, Jobs (job→steps tree), and Log (tail/follow with polling for active jobs).\n- Registers the page in the app (page list, keymap/config loader tests) and adds UI support (header + status bar).\n- Updates default config, docs, and demo tape/GIF to document and showcase the new view.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-actions.tape | Adds a VHS demo script to record the Actions view GIF. |\r\n| src/main.rs | Registers the `actions` module and appends the Actions page to the page list. |\r\n| src/github/domain/disk_cache.rs | Makes cache helpers `pub(crate)` so the Actions page can reuse them. |\r\n| src/github/domain/client.rs | Makes `run_gh` / `run_gh_json` `pub(crate)` for reuse by the Actions client. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Adds Actions header/status bar rendering functions. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Adds `actions_page()` config loader + tests; updates app keymap test page list. |\r\n| src/core/app.rs | Updates app keymap resolution test to include Actions as the 5th page and reserve key `6`. |\r\n| src/actions/state.rs | Implements `ActionsState`: background fetch, polling on tick, pane wiring, and page help. |\r\n| src/actions/panes/runs.rs | Implements Runs pane: list, search, selection preservation, browser open. |\r\n| src/actions/panes/jobs.rs | Implements Jobs pane: job→steps tree rows, selection preservation, browser open, open-log focus. |\r\n| src/actions/panes/log.rs | Implements Log pane: TailPane rendering, failed-step jumps, polling/append logic. |\r\n| src/actions/panes/mod.rs | Exposes the Actions panes submodules. |\r\n| src/actions/page.rs | Constructs the Actions page. |\r\n| src/actions/mod.rs | Adds the Actions module structure/exports. |\r\n| src/actions/domain/types.rs | Adds serde types for runs/jobs/steps and `RunState` derivation helpers. |\r\n| src/actions/domain/time.rs | Adds ISO8601 parsing + duration/relative-time formatting utilities. |\r\n| src/actions/domain/log.rs | Adds job log parsing (gh tab columns vs REST) + ANSI stripping + tail diffing. |\r\n| src/actions/domain/client.rs | Adds `gh run` / `gh api` wrappers and run-list disk caching. |\r\n| src/actions/domain/mod.rs | Exposes the Actions domain submodules. |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Adds `page \"actions\"` layout/keys and binds key `6` to `page:actions`. |\r\n| assets/demo-actions.gif | Adds the recorded Actions demo GIF (via Git LFS pointer). |\r\n| README.md | Documents the Actions view, keys, and demo GIF. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Adds Japanese documentation for the Actions view and its keys. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Documents the new `actions` page name and pane actions. |\r\n| mise.toml | Adds `demo:actions` and includes it in `demo:all`. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/25 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 3\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:40:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"eb8f4d99866d627472f22558aa509eca1adbc138"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPjQuA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThere’s at least one user-visible correctness issue (status bar “in progress” label includes queued runs) plus a misleading comment that should be corrected for accuracy.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/core/ui/status_bar.rs:316**\n* The status bar label says \"in progress\", but `ActionsState::counts()` treats both queued and in-progress runs as \"active\" (`RunState::is_active()` includes `Queued`). This can misreport queued-only runs as \"in progress\".\n```\n                format!(\"◐ {active} in progress\"),\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/25 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:48:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"93b027d3829db618bf7b3f34ea9c8e992151545c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPm6WQ","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"93b027d3829db618bf7b3f34ea9c8e992151545c"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPm7NA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dadc84f9f9949d830d368b6f426cc2439ba26ea2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPm8Ig","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dadc84f9f9949d830d368b6f426cc2439ba26ea2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPm89A","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dadc84f9f9949d830d368b6f426cc2439ba26ea2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLPpLJA","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🔵 Needs a closer look\n\nThe log pane can start a “final fetch” while a poll fetch is still in flight, allowing out-of-order responses to overwrite a complete log with a partial one.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**Previously missed (1)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**src/actions/panes/log.rs:170**\n* `update_target()` can start a “final fetch” when a job transitions from in-progress to completed, even if a poll fetch is already in flight. Because both requests share the same `request_id`, whichever response arrives last wins; an older poll response arriving after the final full fetch could overwrite the complete log with a partial one.\n\nTo avoid this race, invalidate any in-flight request before starting the final fetch (bump `request_id`), and consider forcing `append = false` for the final full fetch so the buffer is replaced deterministically.\n```\n    pub fn update_target(&mut self, latest: LogTarget, tx: &mpsc::Sender<ActionsBgMessage>) {\n        let Some(current) = &self.target else {\n            return;\n        };\n        if current.job_id != latest.job_id {\n            return;\n        }\n        let finished = current.in_progress && !latest.in_progress;\n        self.target = Some(latest);\n        if finished {\n            self.spawn(tx, true);\n        }\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 25/25 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-28T09:02:03Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"dadc84f9f9949d830d368b6f426cc2439ba26ea2"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:24:16Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299121585/job/99223835013","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:24:26Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:58:18Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33157354891/job/98803210062","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:58Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:57:23Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33157354882/job/98803209619","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:58Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:57:54Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33157354891/job/98803209923","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:57:00Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:59:15Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33157354891/job/98803210072","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:57:00Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:59:15Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33157354891/job/98803707115","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:59:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:24:16Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299121585/job/99223819364","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:24:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:57:48Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33157354882/job/98803209828","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:58Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-28T08:58:19Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33157354882/job/98803209796","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-28T08:56:59Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-30T07:24:16Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33299121585/job/99223819414","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-30T07:24:16Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"✨ Actions view: workflow runs, jobs and job log"}
